## What Problem This Solves

In `extensions/telegram/src/send.ts`, `withTelegramApiContextLease` accepted a
`Promise<T>` as its second argument. The inner operation
(`sendMessageTelegramWithContext`, etc.) was evaluated **synchronously** as a
function argument before `withTelegramApiContextLease` was entered. Any
synchronous exception thrown during that evaluation — from the preamble of the
async function (destructuring, token resolution, target parsing) or from
`resolveTelegramApiContext` which acquires the lease via `client.lease?.()` —
propagated before the `.finally()` release wrapper was attached, leaking the
client options lease.

## Root Cause

```ts
// Before (broken)
function withTelegramApiContextLease<T>(context, operation: Promise<T>): Promise<T> {
  return operation.finally(() => context.clientOptionsLease?.release());
}

export async function sendMessageTelegram(to, text, opts) {
  const context = resolveTelegramApiContext(opts);  // acquires lease
  return withTelegramApiContextLease(
    context,
    sendMessageTelegramWithContext(to, text, opts, context),  // evaluated BEFORE lease wrapper
  );
}
```

## Fix

Change `withTelegramApiContextLease` to accept a thunk `() => Promise<T>` and
call it inside a try-catch. All 13 call sites updated to pass `() => expr`
instead of `expr`.

```ts
// After (fixed)
function withTelegramApiContextLease<T>(context, operation: () => Promise<T>): Promise<T> {
  try {
    return operation().finally(() => context.clientOptionsLease?.release());
  } catch (err) {
    context.clientOptionsLease?.release();
    throw err;
  }
}

export async function sendMessageTelegram(to, text, opts) {
  const context = resolveTelegramApiContext(opts);
  return withTelegramApiContextLease(context, () =>
    sendMessageTelegramWithContext(to, text, opts, context),
  );
}
```

## Evidence

### Vitest (same 10 pre-existing failures on main)

```
 Test Files  1 failed (1)
      Tests  10 failed | 163 passed (173)
```

The 10 failures exist identically on `main` — not introduced by this change.

### Call sites updated (13 total)

`sendMessageTelegram`, `sendLocationTelegram`, `sendTypingTelegram`,
`reactMessageTelegram`, `deleteMessageTelegram`, `pinMessageTelegram`,
`unpinMessageTelegram`, `editForumTopicTelegram`, `editMessageReplyMarkupTelegram`,
`editMessageTelegram`, `createForumTopicTelegram`, `sendPollTelegram`,
`sendWithChatActionTelegram`

